# A Shared value's field is written with values of its type (§19.1, §10.2), whole or in part, and is
# read through `->`, never `.`; only a shared struct has a value behind it. A shared struct's value
# passed by `&` is a copy for the call (§7.3): never to an async function, and never beside
# another place reached through a shared struct, since two handles may be one.

